## vm.args of the Burrito-wrapped `nobi` binary (mix nobi.dist).
## The plain release keeps Mix's default vm.args.

## Ctrl-C stops `nobi start` (the VM halts) instead of opening the BEAM's
## BREAK menu. SQLite keeps every committed write across a halt.
+Bd

## Burrito's wrapper runs
##   erlexec -s elixir start_cli -boot start ... -args_file vm.args ... -extra <argv>
## and erlexec puts the plain arguments after `-extra` in this file BEFORE the
## command line's. Elixir's CLI then sees
##   -e Nobi.CLI.main(System.argv()) -- <argv>
## so it evaluates the one CLI entry with System.argv() = <argv>. The `--`
## keeps Elixir from reading <argv> itself (`--version`, `-h`, or a word it
## would run as a script file). The release boots Nobi with `:load` only;
## Nobi.CLI.main/1 starts it through Nobi.Release.start/0 for `start`.
## The expression must contain no whitespace (args files split on it).
## Everything after `-extra` is a plain argument, so it stays the last line.
-extra -e Nobi.CLI.main(System.argv()) --
